From 84f8cd9d250645b60e94afc89baf92d2678b5631 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:22:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban CI progress: unreadable-runner fallback scans
 every in-progress run for the pool's job (#2235 post-merge)

Found by post-merge check t_01a1d525bf173713 of PR #2235 (card t_01a1d52e85d1d757).

Defect: with both runner lists unreadable, `_recent_job_on` read the jobs of only
the first RECENT_RUNS_MAX=4 runs of `actions/runs?status=in_progress&per_page=10`.
On 2026-11-13 ~13:50 example-org/hermes had 23 in-progress runs, and
the one whose job held the only hermes-state runner (run 43436108829, `CI`, job on
mini-hermes-state-1) was 21st. Queued run 43434396722 (`hermes-sync macOS (real
codesign)`, labels self-hosted,macOS,hermes-state, queued 1035 s) read
`not_starting` with `fetch_runners=lambda _r: None`: the wake + runners-offline
assertion #2235 exists to prevent.

Why a deeper scan, not a filter: GitHub has no jobs-by-label query, the run list
order says nothing about which run holds a runner, and the holding run was of
another workflow than the queued one, so a same-workflow filter would also have
missed it. So:

- every in-progress run (one list call, per_page=100, up to IN_PROGRESS_RUNS_MAX=40)
  has its jobs read, then up to RECENT_RUNS_MAX=4 recently completed runs as before;
  the queued run itself is skipped (its jobs were already checked);
- the job lists are read POOL_SCAN_READERS=6 at a time: each read is a broker vend
  plus a gh call (~3 s measured on a worker), so 23 sequential reads would eat most
  of the 90 s sweep budget; the deadline is checked before every list read and every
  batch, so OverBudget/deferred behaviour is unchanged;
- one scan's answer is kept POOL_SCAN_TTL_SECONDS (60 s) per (repo, labels), so
  cards waiting on the same pool share it; an unreadable list or job read is not
  remembered (no evidence either way), and a read error in one run does not hide a
  match in another.

Live (read-only, same worker, same minute): base `_recent_job_on` for
self-hosted,macOS,hermes-state -> '' (10 calls, 29 s); fixed -> 'runner
mini-hermes-state-1 took job 131929660032' (23 calls, 19 s). Full no-match scan for
self-hosted,ci-fast: 24 calls, 23 s.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_ci_progress.py), each proven red on its mutant:
- pool's running job in the 21st of 26 in-progress runs -> busy (red on base and
  with IN_PROGRESS_RUNS_MAX=4);
- M1 (`elif` -> `if` on the fallback): both runner lists read, only runner offline,
  a running job on the labels -> still not_starting, no run list read;
- M4 (drop `in_progress or`): an in-progress job started 40 min ago -> busy;
- the shared scan: second card reads no run list; expiry rescans; the queued run is
  not read twice;
- budget cut mid-scan -> deferred, nothing remembered; unreadable run list not
  remembered; one 502 job list with/without a match elsewhere; the six reads of a
  batch are in flight together (barrier; red with POOL_SCAN_READERS=1).
